# Git push policy

When you finish a substantive task that changes tracked project files (especially under `fic-react/`):

1. Run `git status` and include all relevant changes (no secrets: `.env`, credentials).
2. Create a clear commit with a focused message (why, not just what).
3. Push `main` to **both** remotes unless the user says otherwise:
   - `origin` → `https://github.com/MAbdullahAbbasi/ficonsultancy.git`
   - `ficonsultancys` → `https://github.com/MAbdullahAbbasi/ficonsultancys.git`

Do not force-push to `main`. Do not skip hooks unless the user explicitly asks.

If there is nothing to commit, say so; do not create empty commits.
